1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:04,580
November 17th, 2018, the day of the Yellow Vests protests.

2
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:09,260
Since I’ve always been politically engaged, I told myself I had to do something.

3
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:12,020
So I built this hand in four days,

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,160
using only scrap metal I had collected from nearby farmers.

5
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:24,980
And I built it on the pétanque field without asking anyone for permission.

6
00:00:25,420 --> 00:00:31,760
The mayor came by, saw it, and practically bought it before it was even finished.

7
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:35,080
I made it there and intended to leave it there.

8
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:39,540
So what does this outstretched hand represent?

9
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:41,780
An outstretched hand.

10
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:44,900
An outstretched hand.

11
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:49,900
But the hand is also a very particular symbol.

12
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:53,980
It can represent many different things.

13
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:56,900
It is something that connects us.

14
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,500
It is something we extend.

15
00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:01,340
It is something we give.

16
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:03,160
It is something we receive.

17
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:07,440
It is something through which we project our humanity.

18
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,940
It helps us work as much as it helps us meet other people.

19
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:17,400
The material you use, does it already carry life within it?

20
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:18,580
In fact, it does have a life.

21
00:01:19,630 --> 00:01:21,000
All the little dents you see there,

22
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:22,900
all those little marks,

23
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:26,920
on a piece like the hand, they create something special.

24
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:30,360
If it had been made from new metal, it would not have been as beautiful.

25
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,440
So you are giving them a second life.

26
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:34,040
Absolutely, that is exactly it.

27
00:01:34,310 --> 00:01:40,020
You see, look, there are old clocks here.

28
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:43,080
Old gears like these are magnificent.

29
00:01:43,310 --> 00:01:44,400
And they can still be used.

30
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:51,660
I have old hammers, old shovels, pickaxes, anything you can imagine.

31
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:58,160
And yes, by reusing them, you could say it gives them a new life.

32
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:01,300
That is what really gets people thinking.

33
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:06,420
When you see something all brown and seemingly unremarkable,

34
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:13,040
and inside it there are little details that suddenly catch your eye.

35
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:13,740
That is what makes it beautiful.